{# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Proxmox per-node health (index=os_proxmox sourcetype=pve:health).

   Zammad #1000415: a node's I/O pressure stall (PSI) climbing and staying
   high is the earliest visible symptom of a saturated backing disk — it
   shows up here before the ZFS pool that caused it is ever queried
   directly. The event is syslog-wrapped (same shape as index=openbao_audit
   in the splunk-homelab skill notes): sourcetype=pve:health is set, but the
   key=value pairs sit in _raw and are NOT field-extracted, so a bare
   `psi_io_avg60=*` search matches nothing and reads exactly like "no such
   field" — verified against live 2026-09-19 events. `rex` pulls it out
   below.

   pve-health emits roughly once a minute per host (measured cadence 60-65s,
   2026-09-19). "3 consecutive samples" is read literally as the 3 most
   recent events for that host, not a fixed time window, so a slow or
   delayed emitter does not silently satisfy the condition with fewer than
   3 real samples — `where samples>=3` guards that.

   No pool allocation / fragmentation metric exists anywhere in Splunk for
   this estate (checked index=os_proxmox and index=hardware, 2026-09-19) —
   pve-health does not emit it and no other sourcetype does either. That
   alert is NOT added here; it needs pve-health (or a sibling exporter) to
   start emitting pool alloc%/frag% before Splunk can see it at all.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
[proxmox_node_io_pressure_sustained]
description = Fires when a Proxmox node's I/O pressure-stall average (psi_io_avg60, from pve-health) has been over 25% for its last 3 consecutive samples (~3 min at the ~60s emit cadence). Sustained I/O pressure is the earliest visible symptom of a saturated backing disk — this is what a full/fragmented ZFS pool looks like from the node's own scheduler before the pool itself is ever queried (Zammad #1000415).
search = index=os_proxmox sourcetype=pve:health \
| rex field=_raw "psi_io_avg60=(?<psi_io_avg60>[\d.]+)" \
| sort 0 host, -_time \
| streamstats count AS sample_n BY host \
| where sample_n<=3 \
| stats count AS samples, count(eval(psi_io_avg60>25)) AS high_samples, latest(psi_io_avg60) AS latest_psi_io_avg60, latest(_time) AS latest_time BY host \
| where samples>=3 AND high_samples=3 \
| eval latest_time=strftime(latest_time, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S") \
| table host, latest_psi_io_avg60, latest_time, samples
dispatch.earliest_time = -6m
dispatch.latest_time = now
cron_schedule = */2 * * * *
enableSched = 1
is_visible = 1
disabled = 0
alert.severity = 4
alert.suppress = 1
alert.suppress.period = 30m
alert.suppress.fields = host
alert.track = 1
counttype = number of events
relation = greater than
quantity = 0
